//? Title: Scanline fill: actual pixel-center crossings and clipped integer spans
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Rasterize an ordered polygon into unique integer pixels by testing their
centers. Actual row records show intersections and paired spans before the
original square, right triangle and concave arrow fixtures.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

A row y samples ys=y+0.5. An edge crosses when min(ya,yb)<=ys<max(ya,yb), so
horizontal edges do not cross and a shared vertex is counted once. Sort the
actual x intersections and pair them by the even-odd rule. The historical
horizontal endpoint policy emits integer columns
$$ \lceil x_L-0.5\rceil\le x\le\lfloor x_R-0.5\rfloor. $$
\alttext(Columns are included when their center is between the paired horizontal intersections, including both endpoints.)
Candidate rows run from ceil(ymin-0.5) to ceil(ymax-0.5) exclusive. Integer
spans are clipped and unioned before emission. Pixel count is not continuous
area: the original twenty-by-twenty right triangle includes diagonal boundary
centers and yields 210 pixels, although its continuous area is 200.
Intersections use widened floating interpolation, not exact geometric
predicates.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/scanline_fill_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/scanline_fill.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::scanline_fill_trace({{0, 0}, {2, 0}, {2, 2}, {0, 2}});
    std::print("| actual row | sampled center | actual sorted crossings | paired spans | merged spans |\n| " "---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.rows)
        std::print("| {} | {} | `{}` | {} | {} |\n", s.y, s.center, s.crossings,
                   s.paired.size(), s.merged.size());
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Square from (0,0) to (2,2)");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual sampled rows {}", r.scanlines));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual unique pixels {}", r.pixels.size()));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/scanline_fill_tiny.svg");
}
```
