> API and interpretation

The specified horizontal-boundary inclusion is intentional. Fractional minima
now sample every eligible center; output address conversion and integer loops
are checked. Clip geometry before integer casts. Runtime is
O(rows*vertices+crossing sorts+pixels), with independent row, edge, pixel and
capture policies.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Foley, van Dam, Feiner and Hughes, Computer Graphics: Principles and Practice,
  second edition (1990), scan conversion background

